{
  "raw": {
    "https://careers.umass.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-scenic-design-amherst-massachusetts-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Scenic Design",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Scenic Design - Amherst, Massachusetts, United States Assistant Professor of Scenic Design - Amherst, Massachusetts, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Scenic Design 510032 Amherst, Massachusetts, United States College of Humanities & Fine Arts Full Time Tenure Track Faculty Opening on: Oct 14 2026 Closing on: Feb 14 2027 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Assistant Professor of Scenic Design Executive Area: Academic Affairs College/School/MBU: Humanities & Fine Arts Department: Theater Work Location: Amherst Schedule: Full Time Work Arrangement: Onsite Job Summary The University of Massachusetts Amherst Department of Theater seeks a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor of Scenic Design, with the position slated to begin September 1, 2027. The successful candidate will be an artist and teacher whose primary specialty is scenic design, and as a multi-disciplinary artist, has experience and expertise in some other area of theater (for example, other design areas, directing, puppetry, etc.). Reflecting the needs and advances of the industry, a candidate with experience in projection design or other technologies is desirable. The strong candidate will be committed to a student-centered, mentorship model of teaching and learning, with the ability to teach foundational courses, advanced topics (such as computer assisted drafting), and courses that can appeal to the general UMass student body. They should also have significant industry connections that can be an important part of student learning and experiences. The Department seeks a colleague who will contribute to the research and creative mission of a flagship R1 university through an active program of creative and/or scholarly achievement. The successful candidate will demonstrate outstanding potential to establish a sustained record of nationally recognized creative work, research, and professional engagement that will lead to a national and international reputation in scenic design and related fields. We seek an artist-scholar whose professional practice advances the discipline, contributes to contemporary conversations in theater and performance, and creates opportunities for collaboration, visibility, and impact beyond the university. The Department depends on its faculty and staff being flexible, collaborative, communicative, and adventurous, and able to model these traits to the students. We are particularly interested in artists who have diverse expertise or experience in theater-making, adaptable to a range of budgets and spaces, as well as possible experience in other creative industries. The Department of Theater desires a committed colleague who will balance excellence in teaching and mentorship with professional work appropriate for tenure and promotion at a major public research university. Essential Functions This position will teach a 2-2 courseload. In addition to the teaching responsibilities this position is responsible for the scene design, scenic art and properties design of the department's main stage season and the supervision of student designers and artisans. This includes attending design and production meetings as well as design and technical rehearsals. They will collaborate with all areas and work closely with scene shop faculty and staff. The successful candidate will also be responsible for providing service to the department, college, and university; as well as maintaining a robust portfolio of creative achievement. Minimum Qualifications MFA in Design or terminal degree in related field by time of hire. Demonstrated excellence in teaching design at the college level. Substantial experience as a professional designer with evidence of impact in the field. Evidence of a significant and growing record of creative and/or scholarly achievement, with clear potential to achieve national recognition and develop an international reputation appropriate for tenure at a research-intensive university. An ability to collaborate across disciplines and build community partnerships Working knowledge of current and/or emerging design technologies and software, such as digital media or projection design. Additional Details About the Department of Theater The Department of Theater produces high-caliber, artistic creations on stage, telling human stories that connect audiences and performers in our increasingly interconnected, complex world. We model and practice professional theater-making at every level of our teaching and production process. The Department offers a robust undergraduate program, with a BA major, minor, and a Multicultural Theater Certificate, as well as an evolving MFA program. Our productions are a laboratory for our students, and we nurture a strong commitment to community engagement and participation. This position is subject to final budgetary and administrative approval. Working Conditions Work is performed in a standard office or indoor university environment and involves minimal physical exertion. Salary Information The University expects to pay within an approximate range between $79,350 and $125,234 for this position. Salary is commensurate with experience. This position is a 9-month academic year appointment at 100% full-time equivalency with full benefits. Please note: The low end of this range is based on the minimum salary for the rank included in the collective bargaining agreement between the University and the Massachusetts Society of Professors, UMass Amherst/MTA/NEA. The high-end of the pay range reflects an increase above the median salaries at this rank within the department for faculty who may have multiple years of faculty experience. The specific pay for this position will be determined by the University based on consideration of all relevant factors, including faculty rank and required relevant certifications, when and if it decides to extend an offer of employment. Special Instructions for Applicants Please upload your cover letter, resume and/or curriculum vitae, a teaching philosophy statement, a link to your portfolio, along with a completed application and contact information for 3 professional references who are willing to provide letters of reference upon request. Review of applications will begin October 31, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applications received after October 31, 2026 may not be reviewed. If you have questions about this position, please contact the Chair of the Search Committee Professor Christopher Baker via email at cbake1@umass.edu. Additional Information For more information on living, working, and learning in the Pioneer Valley of Massachusetts please visit: https://www.umass.edu/faculty-development/prospective-faculty This position will remain open for the time period required by any applicable collective bargaining agreement and will continue until a suitable candidate pool is identified. Interested applicants are strongly encouraged to apply early. This position will remain open for the time period required by any applicable collective bargaining agreement and will continue until a suitable candidate pool is identified. Interested applicants are strongly encouraged to apply early. Apply Now! Content missing Similar Jobs Assistant Professor of Scenic Design Humanities & Fine Arts The University of Massachusetts Amherst Department of Theater seeks a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor of Scenic Design, with the position slated to begin September 1, 2027. The successful candidate will be an artist and teacher whose primary specialty is scenic design, and as a multi-disciplinary artist, has experience and expertise in some other area of theater (for example, other design areas, directing, puppetry, etc.). Reflecting the needs and advances of the industry, a candidate with experience in projection design or other technologies is desirable. Dining Hall Supervisor (Catering) Auxiliary Enterprises The Dining Hall Supervisor for Catering supervises and participates in the set-up of dining rooms and serving areas; assists in the serving of food and beverage; delivers and services coffee breaks and meals; supervises personnel assigned to the function; assists with maintaining records; trains and supervises student employees. Lecturer/Visiting Assistant Professor College of Natural Sciences The Department of Mathematics and Statistics (www.umass.edu/mathematics-statistics) at the University of Massachusetts Amherst invites applications for Visiting Assistant Professor positions (non-tenure track). One or more appointments may be a Marshall H. Stone Visiting Assistant Professorship, with a higher salary and an enhanced research fund. Candidates should have completed the Ph.D. by the beginning of the appointment. The initial appointment is for one (1) year and is ordinarily renewable for two (2) additional years. Exceptional promise in research and a commitment to outstanding teaching at all levels of the curriculum are expected. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 16bb4d65 Last Name (required) 5d490fe1 Email (required) 78eea217 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://careers.umass.edu/jobs/lecturer-visiting-assistant-professor-amherst-massachusetts-united-states": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Visiting Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Lecturer/Visiting Assistant Professor - Amherst, Massachusetts, United States Lecturer/Visiting Assistant Professor - Amherst, Massachusetts, United States Kiosk mode Lecturer/Visiting Assistant Professor 509964 Amherst, Massachusetts, United States Academic Year (9 Months) College of Natural Sciences Full Time Lecture & Non Tenure-Track MSP On Site Show More Show Less Faculty Opening on: Oct 14 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Lecturer/Visiting Assistant Professor Executive Area: Academic Affairs College/School/MBU: College of Natural Sciences Department: Mathematics & Statistics Work Location: Amherst Schedule: Full Time Work Arrangement: Onsite Job Summary The Department of Mathematics and Statistics (www.umass.edu/mathematics-statistics) at the University of Massachusetts Amherst invites applications for Visiting Assistant Professor positions (non-tenure track). One or more appointments may be a Marshall H. Stone Visiting Assistant Professorship, with a higher salary and an enhanced research fund. Candidates should have completed the Ph.D. by the beginning of the appointment. The initial appointment is for one (1) year and is ordinarily renewable for two (2) additional years. Exceptional promise in research and a commitment to outstanding teaching at all levels of the curriculum are expected. Essential Functions Teaching responsibility of two (2) courses per semester; Marshall H. Stone visiting assistant professorships have reduced teaching loads. Maintain an active research program and contribute to the research life of the department by attending/organizing/giving talks in local seminars, informal mathematical discussions and/or collaborations with faculty, other visiting assistant professors, or graduate students. Contribute to mathematical research in the broader mathematical community by attending research seminars and conferences, publishing research, and presenting research at seminars and conferences. Other Functions Work collaboratively and effectively to promote teamwork, equality and inclusiveness. Work in partnership with colleagues within the CNS community and across the campus to support the Dean’s strategic priorities. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the mission and goals of the College of Natural Sciences. Minimum Qualifications A PhD in mathematics, statistics, or a closely related field by the time of appointment. Exceptional promise in research. Experience in teaching undergraduate math and/or statistics courses and the ability to work with diverse populations of students. A commitment to outstanding teaching at all levels of the curriculum. The potential to interact effectively with department faculty members. Additional Details At UMass Amherst and in CNS, we strive to be a community where every individual feels a sense of belonging, where every individual is included, and where every individual is valued. These values and goals are reflected in the College of Natural Sciences’ Inclusive Excellence framework and in the UMass Amherst’s For the Common Good: 2024–2034 Strategic Plan. This position is subject to final budgetary and administrative approval. Working Conditions Work is performed in a standard office or indoor university environment and involves minimal physical exertion. Work Schedule and Work Arrangement Anticipated start date of September 1, 2027. Monday - Friday, 40 hours per week. Salary Information The University expects to pay within an approximate range between $65,550 and $80,959 for this position. Please note: The low end of this range is based on the minimum salary for the rank included in the collective bargaining agreement between the University and the Massachusetts Society of Professors, UMass Amherst/MTA/NEA. The high-end of the pay range reflects an increase above the median salaries at this rank within the department for faculty who may have multiple years of faculty experience. The specific pay for this position will be determined by the University based on consideration of all relevant factors, including faculty rank and required relevant certifications, when and if it decides to extend an offer of employment. Special Instructions for Applicants To apply, please submit the following required documents: Curriculum vita, a cover letter, a statement of teaching philosophy and experiences, In addition, at least three (3) letters of recommendation must be submitted. Review of applications will begin on December 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position should be directed to the chair of the Search Committee, Eyal Markman (markman@cns.umass.edu). For additional information about the application process contact David Rodriguez (davidrodrigu@umass.edu). This position will remain open for the time period required by any applicable collective bargaining agreement and will continue until a suitable candidate pool is identified. Interested applicants are strongly encouraged to apply early. Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert b5963e8e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Natural Sciences College of Natural Sciences Categories Academic Year (9 Months) College of Natural Sciences Full Time Lecture & Non Tenure-Track MSP On Site Academic Year (9 Months) College of Natural Sciences Full Time Lecture & Non Tenure-Track MSP On Site First Name (required) a679d187 Last Name (required) dd76ee3d Email (required) 184f0941 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant Professor of Scenic Design Humanities & Fine Arts The University of Massachusetts Amherst Department of Theater seeks a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor of Scenic Design, with the position slated to begin September 1, 2027. The successful candidate will be