    "https://careers.umass.edu/jobs/lecturer-in-musicology-amherst-massachusetts-united-states": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Musicology",
      "description": "Lecturer in Musicology - Amherst, Massachusetts, United States Lecturer in Musicology - Amherst, Massachusetts, United States Kiosk mode Lecturer in Musicology 510037 Amherst, Massachusetts, United States College of Humanities & Fine Arts Full Time Lecture & Non Tenure-Track On Site Show More Show Less Faculty Opening on: Oct 13 2026 Closing on: Jan 13 2027 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Lecturer in Musicology Executive Area: Academic Affairs College/School/MBU: Humanities & Fine Arts Department: Music & Dance Work Location: Amherst Schedule: Full Time Work Arrangement: Onsite Job Summary The Department of Music and Dance at the University of Massachusetts Amherst invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track Lecturer in Musicology. We welcome candidates with expertise in any area. Preference will be given to candidates who can teach courses on a broad range of musical traditions, including global, popular, and Western classical. This is a full-time, nine-month, non-tenure track position at the Lecturer rank to begin September 1, 2027. The initial appointment will be for two years. Reappointments in the first four years are at the Dean’s discretion and will be contingent upon both funding availability and satisfactory performance. Essential Functions Teach a 3/3 load (a combination of general education classes, courses for undergraduate music majors, and graduate seminars). Provide service at the department, college, and university level, including serving on committees, mentoring students, and other obligations. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Musicology, Ethnomusicology, or related fields. ABDs will be considered, with degree in hand expected by the time of appointment. Experience teaching courses, including general education classes on global and/or popular musical traditions. Preferred Qualifications Research record of conference presentations and peer-reviewed publications. Additional Details For more information on living, working, and learning in the Pioneer Valley of Massachusetts please visit: https://www.umass.edu/faculty-development/prospective-faculty This position is subject to final budgetary and administrative approval. Working Conditions Work is performed in a standard office or indoor university environment and involves minimal physical exertion. Salary Information The University expects to pay within an approximate range between $65,550 and $85,275 for this position. Salary is commensurate with experience. This position is a 9-month academic year appointment at 100% full-time equivalency with full benefits. Please note: The low end of this range is based on the minimum salary for the rank included in the collective bargaining agreement between the University and the Massachusetts Society of Professors, UMass Amherst/MTA/NEA. The high-end of the pay range reflects an increase above the median salaries at this rank within the department for faculty who may have multiple years of faculty experience. The specific pay for this position will be determined by the University based on consideration of all relevant factors, including faculty rank and required relevant certifications, when and if it decides to extend an offer of employment. Special Instructions for Applicants Along with an employment application, please submit the following initial application materials: - CV - Cover Letter - Contact information, including email addresses, for three professional references who will be willing to submit a letter of reference upon request. Please address your cover letter to the Chair of the Search Committee discussing your interest in the position, teaching philosophy, ability to contribute meaningfully to the present and future activities of the Department of Music and Dance, and how your work as teacher-scholar, academic citizen, and public servant would further the university’s values and goals as outlined in the university’s strategic plan. You can find these values and goals in our strategic plan here: https://www.umass.edu/strategicplan/strategic-plan . The position will remain posted until filled. Review of applications will begin on November 2, 2026. Applications received after this date may not be reviewed. This position is subject to final budgetary and administrative approval. Applicants must be work authorized for employment in the United States on a full-time basis. This position will remain open for the time period required by any applicable collective bargaining agreement and will continue until a suitable candidate pool is identified. Interested applicants are strongly encouraged to apply early. Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert e9179275 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Humanities & Fine Arts Humanities & Fine Arts Categories College of Humanities & Fine Arts Full Time Lecture & Non Tenure-Track On Site College of Humanities & Fine Arts Full Time Lecture & Non Tenure-Track On Site First Name (required) 4a9eb3f4 Last Name (required) 46d5188d Email (required) 14fa03ec Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant Professor of Scenic Design Humanities & Fine Arts The University of Massachusetts Amherst Department of Theater seeks a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor of Scenic Design, with the position slated to begin September 1, 2027. The successful candidate will be an artist and teacher whose primary specialty is scenic design, and as a multi-disciplinary artist, has experience and expertise in some other area of theater (for example, other design areas, directing, puppetry, etc.). Reflecting the needs and advances of the industry, a candidate with experience in projection design or other technologies is desirable. Dining Hall Supervisor (Catering) Auxiliary Enterprises The Dining Hall Supervisor for Catering supervises and participates in the set-up of dining rooms and serving areas; assists in the serving of food and beverage; delivers and services coffee breaks and meals; supervises personnel assigned to the function; assists with maintaining records; trains and supervises student employees. Lecturer/Visiting Assistant Professor College of Natural Sciences The Department of Mathematics and Statistics (www.umass.edu/mathematics-statistics) at the University of Massachusetts Amherst invites applications for Visiting Assistant Professor positions (non-tenure track). One or more appointments may be a Marshall H. Stone Visiting Assistant Professorship, with a higher salary and an enhanced research fund. Candidates should have completed the Ph.D. by the beginning of the appointment. The initial appointment is for one (1) year and is ordinarily renewable for two (2) additional years. Exceptional promise in research and a commitment to outstanding teaching at all levels of the curriculum are expected. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 16493c7b Last Name (required) a1f148f4 Email (required) 13c06058 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the category/categories"
