    "https://careers.umass.edu/jobs/lecturer-100-in-social-thought-and-political-economy-stpec-amherst-massachusetts-united-states": {
      "title": "Lecturer 100% in Social Thought and Political Economy (STPEC)",
      "description": "Lecturer 100% in Social Thought and Political Economy (STPEC) - Amherst, Massachusetts, United States Lecturer 100% in Social Thought and Political Economy (STPEC) - Amherst, Massachusetts, United States Kiosk mode Lecturer 100% in Social Thought and Political Economy (STPEC) 509634 Amherst, Massachusetts, United States College of Social and Behavioral Sciences Lecture & Non Tenure-Track On Site Faculty Opening on: Oct 9 2026 Closing on: Jan 9 2027 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Lecturer 100% in Social Thought and Political Economy (STPEC) Executive Area: Academic Affairs College/School/MBU: Social & Behavioral Sciences Department: STPEC Work Location: Amherst Schedule: Full Time Work Arrangement: Onsite Job Summary The Social Thought and Political Economy Program, an interdisciplinary department in the College of Social and Behavioral Sciences at the University of Massachusetts, Amherst, invites applications for a full-time Lecturer starting in August 2027. Essential Functions The position includes a 3-3 teaching load plus some administrative responsibilities for student mentoring and professional development. Candidates who study materialist feminism as well as those with expertise in teaching writing within a social sciences curriculum or integrating diversity related content into social theory or political economy courses are especially encouraged to apply. Minimum Qualifications Doctorate in Social Science-related field. Evidence of teaching excellence, strong commitment to undergraduate education, and ability to work with diverse populations/students. Additional Details The Social Thought and Political Economy Program (STPEC) is an interdisciplinary undergraduate major in the College of Social and Behavioral Sciences at the University of Massachusetts Amherst. The STPEC Program encourages students to engage in a critical examination of society and to develop their own capacities for critical reading, writing, and thinking. STPEC students cross disciplinary lines to confront fundamental questions often ignored or neglected by traditional academic thought. This position is subject to final budgetary and administrative approval. Working Conditions Work is performed in a standard office or indoor university environment and involves minimal physical exertion. Work Schedule and Work Arrangement This position will start on September 1, 2027, and will initially be for two years. The position is intended to be ongoing, with reappointments and continued employment contingent upon available funding and satisfactory performance. Salary Information The salary range for this position is expected to be between $65,550 and $75,000. The specific pay for this position will be determined by the University based on consideration of all relevant factors when and if it decides to extend an offer of employment. Please note: The low-end of the pay range in all faculty searches at the University of Massachusetts Amherst is the minimum salary for the rank included in the collective bargaining agreement between the University and the Massachusetts Society of Professors, UMass Amherst/MTA/NEA. The high-end of the pay range reflects an increase above the median salaries at this rank within the department for faculty who may have multiple years of faculty experience. Special Instructions for Applicants Applications should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, evidence of teaching excellence, and the names and contact information of at least three references. We will begin reviewing applications on November 15, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Questions may be directed to: Dr. Toussaint Losier, Director of the Social Thought and Political Economy Program, tlosier@umass.edu . This position will remain open for the time period required by any applicable collective bargaining agreement and will continue until a suitable candidate pool is identified. Interested applicants are strongly encouraged to apply early. Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 3fea4ef8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Social & Behavioral Sciences Social & Behavioral Sciences Categories College of Social and Behavioral Sciences Lecture & Non Tenure-Track On Site College of Social and Behavioral Sciences Lecture & Non Tenure-Track On Site First Name (required) 4c418166 Last Name (required) ff116832 Email (required) 5f9109f0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant Professor of Scenic Design Humanities & Fine Arts The University of Massachusetts Amherst Department of Theater seeks a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor of Scenic Design, with the position slated to begin September 1, 2027. The successful candidate will be an artist and teacher whose primary specialty is scenic design, and as a multi-disciplinary artist, has experience and expertise in some other area of theater (for example, other design areas, directing, puppetry, etc.). Reflecting the needs and advances of the industry, a candidate with experience in projection design or other technologies is desirable. Dining Hall Supervisor (Catering) Auxiliary Enterprises The Dining Hall Supervisor for Catering supervises and participates in the set-up of dining rooms and serving areas; assists in the serving of food and beverage; delivers and services coffee breaks and meals; supervises personnel assigned to the function; assists with maintaining records; trains and supervises student employees. Lecturer/Visiting Assistant Professor College of Natural Sciences The Department of Mathematics and Statistics (www.umass.edu/mathematics-statistics) at the University of Massachusetts Amherst invites applications for Visiting Assistant Professor positions (non-tenure track). One or more appointments may be a Marshall H. Stone Visiting Assistant Professorship, with a higher salary and an enhanced research fund. Candidates should have completed the Ph.D. by the beginning of the appointment. The initial appointment is for one (1) year and is ordinarily renewable for two (2) additional years. Exceptional promise in research and a commitment to outstanding teaching at all levels of the curriculum are expected. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) a588c2db Last Name (required) 2185f675 Email (required) cabb4c36 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the category/categories"
