    "https://careers.umass.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-tt-of-educational-leadership-amherst-massachusetts-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (TT) of Educational Leadership",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (TT) of Educational Leadership - Amherst, Massachusetts, United States Assistant Professor (TT) of Educational Leadership - Amherst, Massachusetts, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor (TT) of Educational Leadership 510021 Amherst, Massachusetts, United States College of Education Full Time MSP On Site Tenure Track Show More Show Less Faculty Opening on: Oct 8 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Assistant Professor (TT) of Educational Leadership Executive Area: Academic Affairs College/School/MBU: College of Education Department: Educ Policy Research & Admin Work Location: Amherst Schedule: Full Time Work Arrangement: Onsite Job Summary Seeking applications for a new faculty position – Assistant Professor of Educational Leadership Area of focus: Educational policy and leadership in US K-12 education. The University of Massachusetts Amherst is seeking qualified candidates for a new tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Educational Leadership to join the dedicated and accomplished community of faculty, students, and staff in the Department of Educational Policy, Research, and Administration (EPRA) within the College of Education. The Department of Educational Policy, Research, and Administration (EPRA) is home to the Center for Education Policy, which houses the Massachusetts Consortium for Innovative Education Assessment and the Annual Massachusetts Educator Survey. These and other initiatives position us as active partners with school districts throughout Massachusetts and beyond. Our district partnerships are grounded in the real, articulated needs of schools, with particular emphasis on sustained, job-embedded professional learning for school leaders in areas such as instructional leadership, equity-centered practice, and organizational change. Ideal candidates will demonstrate expertise in education policy and leadership in US K-12 education, with a research agenda that examines pressing problems of K-12 policy, leadership, and practice. We seek scholars whose work generates scholarship that not only advances theory but also informs actionable improvements in educational systems. Candidates should be prepared to contribute to interdisciplinary collaborations and leverage district partnerships to ensure programming is responsive to workforce needs and grounded in practice. Essential Functions Tenure track faculty at the University of Massachusetts are employed for 9-month contracts with opportunities to engage in additional teaching, research, and community service during summer months and intersessions. Tenure track faculty are expected to teach two courses each semester (undergraduate and/or graduate level, in-person and/or online), maintain a robust student advising caseload, have an active research and scholarship agenda that includes procuring external funding, and provide service related to their expertise to the college, university, and community. Minimum Qualifications Successful applicants will have earned a doctorate in Education, Public Policy, or a relevant social science field. They will have broad expertise in education policy and leadership in US K-12 education, with a research agenda that examines pressing problems of K-12 policy, leadership, and/or practice and the ways these issues shape public education. Regardless of their research focus areas, candidates must have experience working on externally funded projects and demonstrate potential to secure external funding. In addition to their research, candidates must demonstrate the ability to teach classes across multiple program levels. Specific teaching responsibilities will include relevant courses in the multi-campus undergraduate certificate in Education Policy, Research, and Leadership; the M.Ed. in Education Policy, Research, and Leadership; and the Ph.D. in Educational Leadership. Preferred Qualifications • A track record of publication in recognized outlets, with a clear research trajectory. • Success in procuring external funding for research initiatives. • An emphasis on educational equity and access, particularly related to underrepresented populations in educational leadership. • Experience with program development and curriculum design at multiple educational levels. • Experience designing or teaching in online or hybrid educational programs. • Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively across departments and with community partners. • A record of effective mentoring and supervision of graduate students and early-career scholars. • Experience with principal licensure programming, including familiarity with licensure requirements and pathways. Additional Details Located in the beautiful Pioneer Valley of Western Massachusetts, the University of Massachusetts Amherst is a leading center of public higher education in the Northeast. Our campus-wide strategic plan calls for our campus community to engage in work “for the common good,” and the College of Education is dedicated to advancing “education for a socially just world.” As the flagship public land-grant university of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts, our mission is to expand educational access, fuel innovation and creativity, and share and use our knowledge for the betterment of society. This position is subject to final budgetary and administrative approval. Working Conditions Work is performed in a standard office or indoor university environment and involves minimal physical exertion. Work Schedule and Work Arrangement This full-time tenure-track position starts on September 1, 2027. Salary Information The University expects to pay within an approximate range between $79,350 and $127,397. Please note: The low end of this range is based on the minimum salary for the rank included in the collective bargaining agreement between the University and the Massachusetts Society of Professors, UMass Amherst/MTA/NEA. The high-end of the pay range reflects an increase above the median salaries at this rank within the department for faculty who may have multiple years of faculty experience. The specific pay for this position will be determined by the University based on consideration of all relevant factors, including faculty rank and required relevant certifications, when and if it decides to extend an offer of employment. Special Instructions for Applicants Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. To ensure consideration for a Winter/Spring interview, we encourage you to apply no later than December 1, 2026. Candidates must provide the following in their application package: 1) Cover letter that lays out your interest in this position and why you are a good fit. 2) Current curriculum vitae. 3) Statement of research outlining your accomplishments briefly, focusing on your future plans and potential fit at UMass Amherst. 4) Statement of teaching, including your teaching philosophy and potential courses you might offer at the undergraduate and graduate levels. 5) Contact information for three professional references. Current and previous UMass employees applying for this position should expect that their past teaching, advising, and service contributions will be reviewed as part of their application. This includes, but is not limited to, review of SRTI scores and comments for each course that was taught. Individuals who have previous experience teaching at another university are strongly encouraged to provide relevant course feedback scores and comments for review by the search committee. This position will remain open for the time period required by any applicable collective bargaining agreement and will continue until a suitable candidate pool is identified. Interested applicants are strongly encouraged to apply early. Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 58f87c36 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Education College of Education Categories College of Education Full Time MSP On Site Tenure Track College of Education Full Time MSP On Site Tenure Track First Name (required) 5b25e3b7 Last Name (required) af292e1d Email (required) 68a91e1d Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant Professor of Scenic Design Humanities & Fine Arts The University of Massachusetts Amherst Department of Theater seeks a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor of Scenic Design, with the position slated to begin September 1, 2027. The successful candidate will be an artist and teacher whose primary specialty is scenic design, and as a multi-disciplinary artist, has experience and expertise in some other area of theater (for example, other design areas, directing, puppetry, etc.). Reflecting the needs and advances of the industry, a candidate with experience in projection design or other technologies is desirable. Dining Hall Supervisor (Catering) Auxiliary Enterprises The Dining Hall Supervisor for Catering supervises and participates in the set-up of dining rooms and serving areas; assists in the serving of food and beverage; delivers and services coffee breaks and meals; supervises personnel assigned to the function; assists with maintaining records; trains and supervises student employees. Lecturer/Visiting Assistant Professor College of Natural Sciences The Department of Mathematics and Statistics (www.umass.edu/mathematics-statistics) at the University of Massachusetts Amherst invites applications for Visiting Assistant Professor positions (non-tenure track). One or more appointments may be a Marshall H. Stone Visiting Assistant Professorship, with a higher salary and an enhanced research fund. Candidates should have completed the Ph.D. by the beginning of the appointment. The initial appointment is for one (1) year and is ordinarily renewable for two (2) additional years. Exceptional promise in research and a commitment to outstanding teaching at all levels of the curriculum are expected. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 5cf40211 Last Name (required) b73dfe8e Email (required) 857173cd Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the category/categories"
