    "https://careers.umass.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-department-of-economics-amherst-massachusetts-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Department of Economics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Department of Economics - Amherst, Massachusetts, United States Assistant Professor - Department of Economics - Amherst, Massachusetts, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor - Department of Economics 509632 Amherst, Massachusetts, United States College of Social and Behavioral Sciences Full Time Hybrid MSP Tenure Track Show More Show Less Faculty Opening on: Oct 6 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Assistant Professor - Department of Economics Executive Area: Academic Affairs College/School/MBU: Social & Behavioral Sciences Department: Economics Work Location: Amherst Schedule: Full Time Work Arrangement: Hybrid Job Summary The Department of Economics at the University of Massachusetts Amherst invites applications for an Assistant Professor appointment expected to start on September 1, 2027. Essential Functions The Department of Economics at the University of Massachusetts Amherst invites applications for an Assistant Professor appointment expected to start on September 1, 2027. Preference will be given to innovative analytical methods, both empirical and theoretical, in a core area such as microeconomics, industrial organization, international trade and finance, and economic history, although economists in all fields are encouraged to apply. UMass Economics has a history and commitment to fostering a wide range of alternative perspectives and rigorous analytic methods for addressing economic challenges in innovative ways. The teaching load is 2/2. Candidates will be judged on their scholarly research, as well as high quality and enthusiastic teaching. A completed Ph.D. in Economics or a closely related field is required by time of appointment. Current or previous external funding, or experience seeking external grants, is a plus. Under exceptional circumstances, highly qualified candidates at other ranks may receive consideration. Minimum Qualifications A Ph.D. in Economics, or a closely related field by the start date of the appointment. Candidates will be judged on their scholarly research, as well as high quality and enthusiastic teaching. Additional Details The Economics faculty members at UMass Amherst work in diverse areas, from heterodox economics, such as Marxian, Post-Keynesian, Neo-Ricardian, Institutionalist, feminist, and stratification economics, to mainstream approaches such as applied microeconomics, economics and philosophy, and general equilibrium theory. The faculty studies economic theory and applied economics related to multiple dimensions of human well-being and social welfare; how economic opportunities are generated and distributed in society; the interplay between power and institutions and between economic behavior and the performance of the economy; and the importance of race, class, and gender. The Department is committed to fostering a diverse faculty, student body, and curriculum. This position is subject to final budgetary and administrative approval. Working Conditions Work is performed in a standard office or indoor university environment and involves minimal physical exertion. Work Schedule and Work Arrangement This position is expected to start on 9/1/27. Salary Information The University of Massachusetts Amherst expects to pay within an approximate range between $79,350 and $168,797 for this position. Please note: The low-end of the pay range in all faculty searches at the University of Massachusetts Amherst is the minimum salary for the rank included in the collective bargaining agreement between the University and the Massachusetts Society of Professors, UMass Amherst/MTA/NEA. The high-end of the pay range reflects an increase above the median of salaries at this rank within the department for faculty who may have multiple years of faculty experience. The specific pay for this position will be determined by the University based on consideration of all relevant factors, including faculty rank and required relevant certifications, when and if it decides to extend an offer of employment. Special Instructions for Applicants Applicants must apply through the UMass online application system unless they are unable to do so. Applicants should submit: 1. A letter of interest addressed to Professor Mwangi wa Gĩthĩnji, Chair, Department of Economics (Crotty Hall, 412 North Pleasant Street, Amherst, MA 01002, USA). 2. Curriculum vitae. 3. One recent research paper. 4. Evidence of teaching effectiveness. 5. Names and contact information for three references who are willing to submit letters upon request through the UMass online application system. 6. A teaching statement that discusses: the candidate’s skills, experiences and commitment to teaching and mentoring diverse and historically underrepresented student populations. Review of applications will begin on November 15, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Preference will be given to applications received on or before November 15, 2026. Selected candidates will be interviewed remotely beginning in December 2026, with campus visits beginning after January 11, 2027. Questions can be addressed to hiring@econs.umass.edu . This position will remain open for the time period required by any applicable collective bargaining agreement and will continue until a suitable candidate pool is identified. Interested applicants are strongly encouraged to apply early. Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 0fed4ded Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Social & Behavioral Sciences Social & Behavioral Sciences Categories College of Social and Behavioral Sciences Full Time Hybrid MSP Tenure Track College of Social and Behavioral Sciences Full Time Hybrid MSP Tenure Track First Name (required) 415100ca Last Name (required) 549d4fd5 Email (required) 44