    "https://careers.umass.edu/jobs/lecturer-in-landscape-architecture-and-regional-planning-100-amherst-massachusetts-united-states": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Landscape Architecture and Regional Planning (100%)",
      "description": "Lecturer in Landscape Architecture and Regional Planning (100%) - Amherst, Massachusetts, United States Lecturer in Landscape Architecture and Regional Planning (100%) - Amherst, Massachusetts, United States Kiosk mode Lecturer in Landscape Architecture and Regional Planning (100%) 509629 Amherst, Massachusetts, United States Academic Year (9 Months) College of Social and Behavioral Sciences Full Time MSP On Site Tenure Track Show More Show Less Faculty Opening on: Sep 2 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Lecturer in Landscape Architecture and Regional Planning (100%) Executive Area: Academic Affairs College/School/MBU: Social & Behavioral Sciences Department: Landscape Arch & Regional Plan Work Location: Amherst Schedule: Full Time Work Arrangement: Onsite Job Summary The Department of Landscape Architecture and Regional Planning (LARP) invites applications for a full-time Lecturer in Landscape Architecture expected to start on September 1, 2027. Essential Functions We are looking for an inspiring individual to serve as teacher, mentor and leader in our professional accredited Landscape Architecture programs. Teaching responsibilities include a 3:3 teaching load. We are particularly interested in applicants capable of teaching a variety of undergraduate landscape architecture studios as well as any one of several possible mixed undergraduate/graduate seminars -- such as a professional practice seminar, graphics/digital technologies, landscape history & theory, construction/ materials, or other topics that suit the specialties and interests of the selected candidate. LARP faculty also mentor graduate and honors students on their capstone projects and serve as guest critics in other studios. All classes are taught in-person at our flagship campus in Amherst. The selected candidate will also serve as director and primary advisor for students in our Bachelor of Science in Landscape Architecture (BSLA) undergraduate program. Typical responsibilities include advising majors on course offering and scheduling, career advice, curricular development, helping promote LARP and our landscape architecture program(s), as well as periodically preparing materials for accreditation and internal reporting. Workload and course assignments will be adjusted to commensurate with service responsibilities associated with directing the BSLA undergraduate program. Should those administrative responsibilities change or be reassigned, the teaching load will return to the standard 3:3. Minimum Qualifications Applicants must have an MLA as of September 1, 2027, as well as at least five years of experience in Landscape Architecture or a closely related profession. As this position would bring fresh, relevant perspectives into the classroom while strengthening our connections to practice and emerging technologies. The ideal candidate is expected to demonstrate evidence of teaching effectiveness; a strong commitment to pedagogical innovation and adaptation; the ability to work collaboratively with others; and a deep interest in advancing student success. Preferred Qualifications Studio and classroom teaching experience in a research university setting is strongly preferred. Professional or academic experience relevant to advising students and directing an academic program is also strongly preferred. Relevant professional experience in Landscape Architecture, including licensure, is a plus. Additional Details LARP is committed to building a vibrant and inclusive academic community. We welcome candidates whose work demonstrates commitment to student success, community engagement, teaching excellence, and service to the department and profession. We seek candidates with a demonstrated ability to engage students from diverse backgrounds and to contribute to a learning environment that supports all students. This position is subject to final budgetary and administrative approval. Working Conditions Work is performed in a standard office or indoor university environment and involves minimal physical exertion. Work Schedule and Work Arrangement This position will start on September 1, 2027, and will initially be for two years. The position is intended to be ongoing, with reappointments and continued employment contingent upon available funding and satisfactory performance. Salary Information The salary range for this position is expected to be between $65,550 and $96,196. The specific pay for this position will be determined by the University based on consideration of all relevant factors when and if it decides to extend an offer of employment. Please note: The low-end of the pay range in all faculty searches at the University of Massachusetts Amherst is the minimum salary for the rank included in the collective bargaining agreement between the University and the Massachusetts Society of Professors, UMass Amherst/MTA/NEA. The high-end of the pay range reflects an increase above the median salaries at this rank within the department for faculty who may have multiple years of faculty experience. Special Instructions for Applicants Application Instructions Along with the application, please submit the following materials: (a) letter of interest, (b) curriculum vitae or resume, teaching (c) professional statement (describing experience, philosophy, and future outlook), (d) teaching evaluations and students’ testimonies (if available), and (e) names and contact information for three references who are willing to submit letters upon request through the UMass online application system. Review of applications will begin on November 3, 2026 , and preference will be given to applications received on or before this date. This position will remain open for the time period required by any applicable collective bargaining agreement and will continue until a suitable candidate pool is identified. Interested applicants are strongly encouraged to apply early. Candidates will interview remotely beginning in December 2026, with campus visits beginning after January 7, 2027. Please direct any questions to Robert Ryan, LARP Search Committee Chair at rlryan@larp.umass.edu . This position will remain open for the time period required by any applicable collective bargaining agreement and will continue until a suitable candidate pool is identified. Interested applicants are strongly encouraged to apply early. Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 48e07fbf Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Social & Behavioral Sciences Social & Behavioral Sciences Categories Academic Year (9 Months) College of Social and Behavioral Sciences Full Time MSP On Site Tenure Track Academic Year (9 Months) College of Social and Behavioral Sciences Full Time MSP On Site Tenure Track First Name (required) f2391dab Last Name (required) 68abba4a Email (required) af313826 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant Professor of Scenic Design Humanities & Fine Arts The University of Massachusetts Amherst Department of Theater seeks a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor of Scenic Design, with the position slated to begin September 1, 2027. The successful candidate will be an artist and teacher whose primary specialty is scenic design, and as a multi-disciplinary artist, has experience and expertise in some other area of theater (for example, other design areas, directing, puppetry, etc.). Reflecting the needs and advances of the industry, a candidate with experience in projection design or other technologies is desirable. Dining Hall Supervisor (Catering) Auxiliary Enterprises The Dining Hall Supervisor for Catering supervises and participates in the set-up of dining rooms and serving areas; assists in the serving of food and beverage; delivers and services coffee breaks and meals; supervises personnel assigned to the function; assists with maintaining records; trains and supervises student employees. Lecturer/Visiting Assistant Professor College of Natural Sciences The Department of Mathematics and Statistics (www.umass.edu/mathematics-statistics) at the University of Massachusetts Amherst invites applications for Visiting Assistant Professor positions (non-tenure track). One or more appointments may be a Marshall H. Stone Visiting Assistant Professorship, with a higher salary and an enhanced research fund. Candidates should have completed the Ph.D. by the beginning of the appointment. The initial appointment is for one (1) year and is ordinarily renewable for two (2) additional years. Exceptional promise in research and a commitment to outstanding teaching at all levels of the curriculum are expected. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 48388281 Last Name (required) c3c3ccfd Email (required) d8b14e57 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the category/categories"
