    "https://careers.umass.edu/jobs/sociology-lecturer-pool-search-amherst-massachusetts-united-states": {
      "title": "Sociology Lecturer Pool Search",
      "description": "Sociology Lecturer Pool Search - Amherst, Massachusetts, United States Sociology Lecturer Pool Search - Amherst, Massachusetts, United States Kiosk mode Sociology Lecturer Pool Search 509618 Amherst, Massachusetts, United States College of Social and Behavioral Sciences Lecture & Non Tenure-Track MSP On Site Part Time Show More Show Less Faculty Opening on: Aug 28 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Sociology Lecturer Pool Search Executive Area: Academic Affairs College/School/MBU: Social & Behavioral Sciences Department: Sociology Work Location: Amherst Schedule: Part Time Work Arrangement: Onsite Job Summary The Department of Sociology at the University of Massachusetts Amherst https://www.umass.edu/sociology/ is seeking to build a pool of non-tenure track adjunct faculty members who can teach one or two on-campus, in-person courses for the Department during the Spring 2027 semester, or future academic term(s). The possibility of teaching additional courses in future semesters is dependent upon funding, departmental instructional need and candidate availability. The Department is seeking candidates with experience in teaching Sociology and related courses. Potential courses for the academic year may include large introductory courses, statistics, and specialized courses in the areas of race and racism, deviance, and gender. Essential Functions Workload will consist of: Teaching undergraduate sociology course(s) Mentoring/advising undergraduates Maintaining your Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA) certification each semester. Contacting the Department Chair within 24 hours with any student concerns or issues. Checking UMass email every 24 business hours during the semester you are teaching. Responding to UMass student email within 24 business hours. Minimum Qualifications Candidates must have a Ph.D. in Sociology or a related field, or a master’s with commensurate professional experience. Successful candidates will demonstrate strong verbal and written communication skills, as well as the ability to work with diverse populations and experience mentoring/advising undergraduates. Visit our website https://www.umass.edu/sociology/ for more information about the department. Working Conditions Work is performed in a standard office or indoor university environment and involves minimal physical exertion. Work Schedule and Work Arrangement Teaching schedules may vary from one semester to another, depending on program needs, resource availability, and enrollment demand. The Department Chair and Academic Program Manager will assign workloads and schedules each semester. Salary Information Total salary $8,195 per course Special Instructions for Applicants To apply, please submit your application online and include the following materials: (a) letter of interest identifying your Sociology subject teaching areas of interest/expertise and (b) curriculum vitae or resume and (c) the names and contact information for three (3) professional references. Please address any questions to the Department Chair, David Cort dcort@soc.umass.edu . We will review applications until positions are filled. Applicants should be aware that a teaching assignment is not guaranteed and that assignments may not be offered in the order candidates enter the pool, as openings for different classes occur at different times. While our in- person and online programs operate year-round, our primary needs are during the fall and spring semesters on the Amherst campus. This position will remain open for the time period required by any applicable collective bargaining agreement and will continue until a suitable candidate pool is identified. Interested applicants are strongly encouraged to apply early. Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert dc360b4f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Social & Behavioral Sciences Social & Behavioral Sciences Categories College of Social and Behavioral Sciences Lecture & Non Tenure-Track MSP On Site Part Time College of Social and Behavioral Sciences Lecture & Non Tenure-Track MSP On Site Part Time First Name (required) 50004e26 Last Name (required) 8f58c068 Email (required) 1427d7d0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant Professor of Scenic Design Humanities & Fine Arts The University of Massachusetts Amherst Department of Theater seeks a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor of Scenic Design, with the position slated to begin September 1, 2027. The successful candidate will be an artist and teacher whose primary specialty is scenic design, and as a multi-disciplinary artist, has experience and expertise in some other area of theater (for example, other design areas, directing, puppetry, etc.). Reflecting the needs and advances of the industry, a candidate with experience in projection design or other technologies is desirable. Dining Hall Supervisor (Catering) Auxiliary Enterprises The Dining Hall Supervisor for Catering supervises and participates in the set-up of dining rooms and serving areas; assists in the serving of food and beverage; delivers and services coffee breaks and meals; supervises personnel assigned to the function; assists with maintaining records; trains and supervises student employees. Lecturer/Visiting Assistant Professor College of Natural Sciences The Department of Mathematics and Statistics (www.umass.edu/mathematics-statistics) at the University of Massachusetts Amherst invites applications for Visiting Assistant Professor positions (non-tenure track). One or more appointments may be a Marshall H. Stone Visiting Assistant Professorship, with a higher salary and an enhanced research fund. Candidates should have completed the Ph.D. by the beginning of the appointment. The initial appointment is for one (1) year and is ordinarily renewable for two (2) additional years. Exceptional promise in research and a commitment to outstanding teaching at all levels of the curriculum are expected. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 6b60dc43 Last Name (required) 4ab454f8 Email (required) 96a845a7 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the category/categories"
