    "https://careers.umass.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-department-of-anthropology-amherst-massachusetts-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Department of Anthropology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Department of Anthropology - Amherst, Massachusetts, United States Assistant Professor - Department of Anthropology - Amherst, Massachusetts, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor - Department of Anthropology 509522 Amherst, Massachusetts, United States College of Social and Behavioral Sciences Full Time Hybrid MSP Tenure Track Show More Show Less Faculty Opening on: Jul 31 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Title: Assistant Professor - Department of Anthropology Executive Area: Academic Affairs College/School/MBU: Social & Behavioral Sciences Department: Anthropology Work Location: Amherst Schedule: Full-time Work Arrangement: Hybrid Job Summary The Department of Anthropology at the University of Massachusetts Amherst invites applications for a tenure-track position at the level of Assistant Professor in Language and Wellbeing, expected to start on September 1, 2027. Essential Functions The Department is seeking a linguistic/cultural anthropologist with a strong record of research that addresses how language plays an integral role in shaping wellbeing. We understand wellbeing to include physical and mental health as well as other aspects of human flourishing, especially in relation to social, environmental, economic, and/or political systems. Areas of focus may include but are not limited to: Biocultural approaches to health and wellbeing Climate change / climate justice Effects of emerging media and technology Healing and belonging in structurally disadvantaged communities Multispecies relations Relationships between science, medicine, and society Applicants should offer evidence of ethnographically grounded research, an innovative theoretical approach, clear plans for future scholarship, and demonstrated excellence in teaching. Regional focus is open. In addition to these areas of specialization, the ideal candidate will value and strengthen links across the sub-fields of anthropology. Current or previous external funding, or experience seeking external grants is a plus. Under exceptional circumstances, candidates at other ranks may receive consideration. Minimum Qualifications A PhD in anthropology or a closely related field is required at or before the time of appointment. Candidates will be judged on their scholarly research record, as well as high quality and enthusiastic teaching. Must be able to teach a large introductory course in linguistic anthropology, a small undergraduate methods course specializing in language and culture, as well as teach and mentor graduate students. Rank and salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Additional Details The Department of Anthropology at UMass Amherst values integrating research and education to address issues of public concern for the common good. We encourage applicants who would contribute to our department’s strong record of using community-based research as the basis for cross-disciplinary collaboration, including through the Center for Braiding Indigenous Knowledges and Science; Demystifying Language Project; Energy Transition Institute; The Ethnography Collective @ UMASS Amherst; Health, Environment, and Arts (HEART) initiative; Institute for Social Science Research; and the Five College Program in Culture, Health, and Science. The teaching load is 2-2. This position is subject to final budgetary and administrative approval. Working Conditions Work is performed in a standard office or indoor university environment and involves minimal physical exertion. Work Schedule and Work Arrangement This full-time tenure-track position starts on September 1, 2027. Salary Information The University of Massachusetts Amherst expects to pay within an approximate range between $79,350 and $123,484 for this position. Please note: The low-end of the pay range in all faculty searches at the University of Massachusetts Amherst is the minimum salary for the rank included in the collective bargaining agreement between the University and the Massachusetts Society of Professors, UMass Amherst/MTA/NEA. The high-end of the pay range reflects an increase above the median of salaries at this rank within the department for faculty who may have multiple years of faculty experience. The specific pay for this position will be determined by the University based on consideration of all relevant factors, including faculty rank and required relevant certifications, when and if it decides to extend an offer of employment. Special Instructions for Applicants Applicants must apply through the UMass online application system unless they are unable to do so. Applicants should submit: A cover letter addressed to Professor Brigitte Holt, Chair, Department of Anthropology, Machmer Hall, 240 Hicks Way, Amherst, MA 01003. Curriculum vitae A one-page research statement that summarizes research scope and trajectory. A one-page teaching philosophy that highlights teaching experience and ability to engage students from diverse backgrounds. Names and contact information for three references. Letters will be requested at a later stage. This information must be submitted through and added to the application in the PageUp online system. Review of applications will begin on October 15, 2026 , and continue until the position is filled. Preference will be given to applications received on or before October 15, 2026. Candidates will interview remotely in December 2026 with campus visits beginning in February 2027. Questions can be addressed to Lynnette Arnold, Chair of the Search Committee at larnold@umass.edu . This position will remain open for the time period required by any applicable collective bargaining agreement and will continue until a suitable candidate pool is identified. Interested applicants are strongly encouraged to apply early. Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 181ef602 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Social & Behavioral Sciences Social & Behavioral Sciences Categories College of Social and Behavioral Sciences Full Time Hybrid MSP Tenure Track College of Social and Behavioral Sciences Full Time Hybrid MSP Tenure Track First Name (required) 7a1d807e Last Name (required) af7db6d9 Email (required) 9e9dbaef Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant Professor of Scenic Design Humanities & Fine Arts The University of Massachusetts Amherst Department of Theater seeks a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor of Scenic Design, with the position slated to begin September 1, 2027. The successful candidate will be an artist and teacher whose primary specialty is scenic design, and as a multi-disciplinary artist, has experience and expertise in some other area of theater (for example, other design areas, directing, puppetry, etc.). Reflecting the needs and advances of the industry, a candidate with experience in projection design or other technologies is desirable. Dining Hall Supervisor (Catering) Auxiliary Enterprises The Dining Hall Supervisor for Catering supervises and participates in the set-up of dining rooms and serving areas; assists in the serving of food and beverage; delivers and services coffee breaks and meals; supervises personnel assigned to the function; assists with maintaining records; trains and supervises student employees. Lecturer/Visiting Assistant Professor College of Natural Sciences The Department of Mathematics and Statistics (www.umass.edu/mathematics-statistics) at the University of Massachusetts Amherst invites applications for Visiting Assistant Professor positions (non-tenure track). One or more appointments may be a Marshall H. Stone Visiting Assistant Professorship, with a higher salary and an enhanced research fund. Candidates should have completed the Ph.D. by the beginning of the appointment. The initial appointment is for one (1) year and is ordinarily renewable for two (2) additional years. Exceptional promise in research and a commitment to outstanding teaching at all levels of the curriculum are expected. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 8539f794 Last Name (required) bbc5cee1 Email (required) a478c6a5 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the category/categories"
